    "created_at": "2026-01-09T15:38:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-09T15:38:04Z",
    "body": "I discovered recently that even Chrome itself is not always cross-platform compatible for the various baselines for a single font. I was trying to write tests using Nato Medium and the rendering differed by several pixels MacOs to Linux, and one or two pixels Windows to Linux (so Windows and MacOS do not match either). This is particularly odd given that the font is loaded from the WPT directory, so is theoretically the same cross-platform.\n\nThere is some testing for this, WPT 2d.text.draw.baseline.*, but it uses a CanvasTest font which presumably has the various baselines consistent across platforms.\n\nThis leads to me to think that maybe the compat problem is at the OS font library level or otherwise below the browser stack. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
